WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.425 --> 00:00:01.824
- Good morning, Believe Nation.

00:00:01.824 --> 00:00:05.570
Today's message is know
what you really want.

00:00:05.570 --> 00:00:07.590
Over to you Alan Watts.

00:00:07.590 --> 00:00:09.390
(rooster crows)

00:00:09.390 --> 00:00:12.307
(upbeat rap music)

00:00:19.451 --> 00:00:21.446
- [Alan Watts] Saint Paul
said that the laborer

00:00:21.446 --> 00:00:23.279
is worthy of his hire.

00:00:25.671 --> 00:00:29.004
And I as a philosopher, mere philosopher

00:00:30.507 --> 00:00:32.590
dealing in higher things,

00:00:33.677 --> 00:00:37.094
always insist that I be paid for my work.

00:00:39.604 --> 00:00:42.604
And I get the highest fee I can get.

00:00:43.560 --> 00:00:46.950
And people say, "Oh you're
just out for money."

00:00:46.950 --> 00:00:50.117
I say, "That's none of your business."

00:00:50.966 --> 00:00:54.264
Because I give most of it away,

00:00:54.264 --> 00:00:57.264
my own needs being extremely simple.

00:00:59.605 --> 00:01:02.428
Although I enjoy good food,

00:01:02.428 --> 00:01:05.261
I don't even own a television set.

00:01:07.400 --> 00:01:11.913
And you know it's a very simple
life but I've got enough.

00:01:11.913 --> 00:01:14.663
And enough is as good as a feast.

00:01:15.824 --> 00:01:18.408
You see a lot of people don't
feel happy unless they have

00:01:18.408 --> 00:01:22.583
another thing beyond money
which is called status.

00:01:22.583 --> 00:01:26.143
And status, to a very large
extent in our economy,

00:01:26.143 --> 00:01:29.143
consists in conspicuous consumption,

00:01:31.949 --> 00:01:34.303
in having this thing and that
thing and the other thing

00:01:34.303 --> 00:01:36.553
and having a swimming pool,

00:01:38.022 --> 00:01:38.855
a Ferrari,

00:01:39.729 --> 00:01:42.945
a certain kind of clothes,
a certain kind of house

00:01:42.945 --> 00:01:46.082
with an enormous
ranch-style picture window

00:01:46.082 --> 00:01:48.487
and so on and so on and so on.

00:01:48.487 --> 00:01:50.524
And we think we need all that

00:01:50.524 --> 00:01:54.227
because we've been persuaded
by a certain kind of propaganda

00:01:54.227 --> 00:01:56.977
that that's how we ought to live.

00:01:58.487 --> 00:02:00.509
Because we haven't been asked ourselves

00:02:00.509 --> 00:02:03.395
whether that was what we really wanted.

00:02:03.395 --> 00:02:05.549
In other words, we've been propagandized

00:02:05.549 --> 00:02:07.977
into thinking what we wanted.

00:02:07.977 --> 00:02:09.111
- I think a lot of people
in entrepreneurship

00:02:09.111 --> 00:02:11.169
are being sold a pipe dream.

00:02:11.169 --> 00:02:13.923
I think a lot of the videos,
a lot of people talking

00:02:13.923 --> 00:02:15.615
about entrepreneurship are talking talking

00:02:15.615 --> 00:02:18.831
about the Entrepreneur
Lifestyle where all you want

00:02:18.831 --> 00:02:20.940
are Ferraris and private jets and islands

00:02:20.940 --> 00:02:23.303
and all of the things that money can buy

00:02:23.303 --> 00:02:25.429
and the path to do that
is entrepreneurship.

00:02:25.429 --> 00:02:26.927
And it's easy to buy into that.

00:02:26.927 --> 00:02:29.303
It's easy to spend money
on courses and programs,

00:02:29.303 --> 00:02:30.553
but it's a lie.

00:02:31.525 --> 00:02:32.883
If you look at the people who have had

00:02:32.883 --> 00:02:34.624
the most success at entrepreneurship,

00:02:34.624 --> 00:02:37.343
none of them had that as their ambition.

00:02:37.343 --> 00:02:39.982
None of the people you look
up to had massive success

00:02:39.982 --> 00:02:43.998
in any industry started
with a dream board,

00:02:43.998 --> 00:02:47.049
a vision board, of having a Ferrari on it.

00:02:47.049 --> 00:02:49.739
If that is your goal,
you will never get there.

00:02:49.739 --> 00:02:53.555
The most successful entrepreneurs
have an absolute passion

00:02:53.555 --> 00:02:58.224
for changing the way something
is done in their industry.

00:02:58.224 --> 00:03:00.832
So you have to tap into what that is.

00:03:00.832 --> 00:03:02.310
Otherwise you're going to fail.

00:03:02.310 --> 00:03:04.510
It's like looking at Lebron
James and seeing this guy

00:03:04.510 --> 00:03:07.916
who has a lot of money,
who's driving nice cars,

00:03:07.916 --> 00:03:09.670
who's wearing nice clothes and like,

00:03:09.670 --> 00:03:11.790
"I want the Lebron James lifestyle.

00:03:11.790 --> 00:03:14.254
"I want to look like, I
want to dress like that guy.

00:03:14.254 --> 00:03:15.668
"I want to be the man like Lebron James

00:03:15.668 --> 00:03:18.153
"when I walk off an airplane
and I'm all pimped out

00:03:18.153 --> 00:03:19.106
"in the latest suit.

00:03:19.106 --> 00:03:20.877
"That's what I want to be like."

00:03:20.877 --> 00:03:23.144
How did Lebron James get there?

00:03:23.144 --> 00:03:25.144
By working his face off.

00:03:26.263 --> 00:03:28.649
By caring about the game of basketball

00:03:28.649 --> 00:03:31.545
and by going all in on that.

00:03:31.545 --> 00:03:33.845
If you look at basketball as a way

00:03:33.845 --> 00:03:37.048
just to make money and
look like Lebron James,

00:03:37.048 --> 00:03:38.331
you will never put in the work

00:03:38.331 --> 00:03:39.880
to actually be great at basketball

00:03:39.880 --> 00:03:41.663
because that's not what you care about.

00:03:41.663 --> 00:03:44.663
Lebron doesn't care about the suits.

00:03:45.574 --> 00:03:49.044
Lebron cares about winning championships

00:03:49.044 --> 00:03:51.589
And the suits are a nice byproduct of it.

00:03:51.589 --> 00:03:53.367
You get the difference?

00:03:53.367 --> 00:03:56.080
Lebron doesn't care about
just getting the next Ferrari

00:03:56.080 --> 00:03:59.437
in his collection or buying
the next shoe that comes out.

00:03:59.437 --> 00:04:01.038
Those are nice perks.

00:04:01.038 --> 00:04:04.177
Not that those are bad but
it's not the ultimate goal.

00:04:04.177 --> 00:04:06.785
The goal is win championships.

00:04:06.785 --> 00:04:08.202
That's what you have to be "all in" at

00:04:08.202 --> 00:04:10.171
if you want to be successful.

00:04:10.171 --> 00:04:12.317
So equate that back to your business.

00:04:12.317 --> 00:04:14.972
If you are starting a business
just to achieve a yacht

00:04:14.972 --> 00:04:17.869
and a Ferrari and a private
island on your vision board,

00:04:17.869 --> 00:04:20.110
you're not going to get there.

00:04:20.110 --> 00:04:21.624
Cause you won't put in the work.

00:04:21.624 --> 00:04:23.848
You have to want to win championships,

00:04:23.848 --> 00:04:27.554
or whatever that equivalent
is, in your industry.

00:04:27.554 --> 00:04:31.075
You want to stomp in your industry.

00:04:31.075 --> 00:04:33.992
And the side benefit of all of that

00:04:35.027 --> 00:04:38.242
is the cars, is the material
wealth, is whatever you want.

00:04:38.242 --> 00:04:40.354
But it can't be number one.

00:04:40.354 --> 00:04:42.463
So I'd encourage you to
dramatically reevaluate

00:04:42.463 --> 00:04:44.630
where your priorities are,

00:04:46.142 --> 00:04:47.882
and until you set them straight,

00:04:47.882 --> 00:04:49.724
you're never going to
achieve what you have

00:04:49.724 --> 00:04:51.109
the potential to achieve.

00:04:51.109 --> 00:04:53.427
So the question today is I'm curious.

00:04:53.427 --> 00:04:55.923
What is the equivalent of
winning championship rings

00:04:55.923 --> 00:04:57.819
in your industry?

00:04:57.819 --> 00:04:59.500
What does that look like for you?

00:04:59.500 --> 00:05:00.761
Leave it in the comments below.

00:05:00.761 --> 00:05:01.881
I'm curious to find out.

00:05:01.881 --> 00:05:04.053
I also want to give a quick
shout out to David Msn.

00:05:04.053 --> 00:05:06.128
David, thank you so much for
picking up a copy of my book

00:05:06.128 --> 00:05:07.132
Your One Word.

00:05:07.132 --> 00:05:08.719
Really means a lot to me man.

00:05:08.719 --> 00:05:10.277
I hope you're enjoying
the read in your planet,

00:05:10.277 --> 00:05:11.522
your life, and your business.

00:05:11.522 --> 00:05:13.021
I appreciate the support.

00:05:13.021 --> 00:05:14.311
Thank you guys again for watching.

00:05:14.311 --> 00:05:15.671
I hope you have an amazing day.

00:05:15.671 --> 00:05:17.990
I believe in you and hope
you continue to believe

00:05:17.990 --> 00:05:20.382
in yourself, and I'll see
you again tomorrow morning

00:05:20.382 --> 00:05:23.300
for another shot of espresso.

00:05:23.300 --> 00:05:26.217
(upbeat rap music)

00:05:31.802 --> 00:05:34.142
- I think people need to
get, sit down and clarify

00:05:34.142 --> 00:05:38.325
what experiences are you really
looking for in your life.

00:05:38.325 --> 00:05:39.788
And that doesn't necessarily
mean, it can include

00:05:39.788 --> 00:05:42.752
lots of money, but it can
also include what do you want

00:05:42.752 --> 00:05:44.671
to experience with that money.

00:05:44.671 --> 00:05:46.482
A sense of freedom, a sense of service,

00:05:46.482 --> 00:05:48.905
a sense of providing value to the world,

00:05:48.905 --> 00:05:52.655
a sense of self-confidence
and self-efficacy.

00:05:54.108 --> 00:05:56.941
What is it that you're after?

00:05:56.941 --> 00:05:59.723
So this in my own
explorations and the whole

00:05:59.723 --> 00:06:02.774
personal growth and self
awareness game for years,

00:06:02.774 --> 00:06:04.539
I've been involved in
that pretty seriously.

00:06:04.539 --> 00:06:07.184
You know there's an exercise
that says, "What do you want?"

00:06:07.184 --> 00:06:08.110
"I want a red Porsche."

00:06:08.110 --> 00:06:10.546
"Great, what experience do you
think that's going to give you?"

00:06:10.546 --> 00:06:13.564
"Freedom and a sense of fun, whatever."

00:06:13.564 --> 00:06:15.115
And then the people get the red Porsche,

00:06:15.115 --> 00:06:17.674
and they're worried about
somebody going to dent it.

00:06:17.674 --> 00:06:20.161
And they can't afford the payments on it.

00:06:20.161 --> 00:06:22.983
They didn't really get the
experience they were looking for.

00:06:22.983 --> 00:06:23.816
What happened?

00:06:23.816 --> 00:06:25.994
They got the symbol,

00:06:25.994 --> 00:06:27.870
but they didn't get the inner experience.

00:06:27.870 --> 00:06:29.794
But if you want the
experience of freedom and fun,

00:06:29.794 --> 00:06:31.512
you can have that this afternoon.

00:06:31.512 --> 00:06:33.046
It doesn't mean you shouldn't
have the red Porsche.

00:06:33.046 --> 00:06:34.612
But it just means that
if you start to focus

00:06:34.612 --> 00:06:36.289
on the inner experience.

00:06:36.289 --> 00:06:38.110
What would climbing the corporate ladder

00:06:38.110 --> 00:06:39.846
give you as an inner experience?

00:06:39.846 --> 00:06:41.092
Why do you want that?

00:06:41.092 --> 00:06:43.042
What's important to you about that?

00:06:43.042 --> 00:06:47.227
And it could be, "I want
to provide for my family

00:06:47.227 --> 00:06:48.894
for after I'm gone."

00:06:50.155 --> 00:06:52.445
So there's a sense of building
wealth or building net worth

00:06:52.445 --> 00:06:56.405
or building assets for people
around you that matter to you.

00:06:56.405 --> 00:06:59.589
There's no right or wrong about
any of your answers to this,

00:06:59.589 --> 00:07:01.649
but I think getting clear about
whether you want to do that

00:07:01.649 --> 00:07:04.162
or whether you want to get there
because you want to be able

00:07:04.162 --> 00:07:07.409
to impact a much larger segment
of the world for doing good,

00:07:07.409 --> 00:07:10.644
or taking it over, I don't
know, for whatever you want.

00:07:10.644 --> 00:07:13.990
But I think that's the key
is being able to externalize

00:07:13.990 --> 00:07:15.847
and start to become objective about, well,

00:07:15.847 --> 00:07:18.469
what is it that you're after.

00:07:18.469 --> 00:07:20.308
Just crafting your own ideal scene

00:07:20.308 --> 00:07:22.519
not only of the things
you want which is fine.

00:07:22.519 --> 00:07:23.659
Don't stop that.

00:07:23.659 --> 00:07:25.250
As a matter of fact,
don't feel embarrassed

00:07:25.250 --> 00:07:26.823
that you want a red Porsche.

00:07:26.823 --> 00:07:28.854
So there's nothing wrong with
any of that material stuff

00:07:28.854 --> 00:07:30.437
that you might want, but it's also true

00:07:30.437 --> 00:07:32.940
that it's a real good idea
to just sit down and say,

00:07:32.940 --> 00:07:34.640
"Let me just lay it out, all out."

00:07:34.640 --> 00:07:38.417
And then use that as a
map to then guide you

00:07:38.417 --> 00:07:41.099
in terms of your
intuitive decision making.

00:07:41.099 --> 00:07:42.740
Don't think you have to
work at it that hard,

00:07:42.740 --> 00:07:44.652
but I think you do need
to be conscious about it

00:07:44.652 --> 00:07:46.791
and validate it in some part of yourself.

00:07:46.791 --> 00:07:48.916
- The difference between
people who are successful

00:07:48.916 --> 00:07:51.185
and not is those who are
successful seem to know

00:07:51.185 --> 00:07:54.367
from the age of seven
or eight, maybe older,

00:07:54.367 --> 00:07:58.359
they're very in tune with what they love.

00:07:58.359 --> 00:08:01.512
I compare it to a voice inside their head,

00:08:01.512 --> 00:08:05.182
not literally a voice,
but something saying

00:08:05.182 --> 00:08:08.076
you really are drawn to this subject.

00:08:08.076 --> 00:08:09.766
And they hear it throughout their life.

00:08:09.766 --> 00:08:13.933
For me, it was writing and
books since I was a kid.

00:08:14.980 --> 00:08:18.897
And you know any time I
deviated from that love

00:08:20.743 --> 00:08:24.237
and went into something
else, I just was so unhappy.

00:08:24.237 --> 00:08:26.559
I knew that I wasn't
doing the right thing.

00:08:26.559 --> 00:08:29.028
And so it's just like this voice
that keeps drawing you back

00:08:29.028 --> 00:08:31.556
to what you really really love.

00:08:31.556 --> 00:08:33.683
- Well, I would say I've always believed

00:08:33.683 --> 00:08:35.879
that a strong mission
statement's really important,

00:08:35.879 --> 00:08:38.877
and I have to say we've
never succeeded at it.

00:08:38.877 --> 00:08:40.553
It's like this odd thing you know.

00:08:40.553 --> 00:08:42.340
We've had 'em every year for 15 years

00:08:42.340 --> 00:08:44.386
and they're constantly different,

00:08:44.386 --> 00:08:45.904
and now we're all so cynical.

00:08:45.904 --> 00:08:47.789
We're like, "Come on we're
trying to make people happy."

00:08:47.789 --> 00:08:51.274
I mean that's the fundamental
thing in a consumer service.

00:08:51.274 --> 00:08:52.641
We're trying to be better,

00:08:52.641 --> 00:08:56.122
and us and Disney and
mission aren't that different

00:08:56.122 --> 00:08:58.069
just a bunch of different tactics at it.

00:08:58.069 --> 00:09:00.188
But we're an emotional product.

00:09:00.188 --> 00:09:04.903
We cater to the things that are
important but not necessary.

00:09:04.903 --> 00:09:07.744
And I love that part about it
cause when you're selling milk

00:09:07.744 --> 00:09:11.299
or penicillin, you're selling
something somebody needs.

00:09:11.299 --> 00:09:14.148
And we get to sell
something you want, okay,

00:09:14.148 --> 00:09:17.048
that you choose to do
because it's really cool.

00:09:17.048 --> 00:09:20.559
It's human to be entertained and connect

00:09:20.559 --> 00:09:23.121
to people over entertainment.

00:09:23.121 --> 00:09:24.969
And so we celebrate that a lot and we want

00:09:24.969 --> 00:09:28.829
to change the industry but in
terms of a mission statement

00:09:28.829 --> 00:09:30.269
like so many companies have ...

00:09:30.269 --> 00:09:33.284
You know Facebook talks
about a more connected

00:09:33.284 --> 00:09:36.841
and open world and you see
that phrase again and again

00:09:36.841 --> 00:09:39.245
and again and it's a powerful mantra.

00:09:39.245 --> 00:09:41.216
We don't have an equivalent and I think

00:09:41.216 --> 00:09:43.316
we probably would have
been stronger if we do.

00:09:43.316 --> 00:09:45.432
In the early days

00:09:45.432 --> 00:09:50.203
it was to connect people
with movies they'll love.

00:09:50.203 --> 00:09:52.049
And it's okay but it's kind of like a long

00:09:52.049 --> 00:09:52.995
kind of awkward phrase,

00:09:52.995 --> 00:09:55.369
connect people with movies they'll love.

00:09:55.369 --> 00:09:57.080
And it's just not punchy.

00:09:57.080 --> 00:10:00.320
And then we used it, we had tee shirts,

00:10:00.320 --> 00:10:02.840
and then it didn't really motivate anyone.

00:10:02.840 --> 00:10:04.249
It didn't really stick.

00:10:04.249 --> 00:10:06.909
But we knew we were trying to
make people happy with DVDs

00:10:06.909 --> 00:10:09.822
and then eventually with
streaming and original content.

